	(text "USB-C (data only) and debug UART"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 172.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2b4c8aa7-0116-5e79-a20e-906adfcee8a4")
	)
	(text "ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N4 (4 MB flash, no PSRAM; PCB antenna).  JLC-assembled (bottom GND pad).\n4 MB = 2 x ~1.9 MB OTA slots (min_spiffs).  -1-N8 is a drop-in if more flash is ever needed.\nSame pad pattern; the -1 footprint outline covers both.  Keep the antenna end clear of copper.\nStrapping: IO0 = BOOT (button), IO3 / IO45 / IO46 left unconnected.\nUSB: data only (native USB-Serial-JTAG).  VBUS feeds only the ESD part; the board\nruns from 12V, so bench programming needs the 12V supply.\nADC1 (IO1-10) for analog; ADC2 is unusable with WiFi.\nADC1: IO1 CP_LVL, IO2 PP_SENSE, IO4/5/10 ANA1-3 (J10), IO6 PAWL_IS, IO7 VSENSE_12V, IO8/9 AIN1/2.\nOpto inputs IO35-38 (active-low), PAWL_INH IO39, status LEDs IO40 / IO21, J10 GPIO IO11 / IO12.\nBOOT / RESET = solder-jumper pads (short with tweezers); USB auto-reset covers normal flashing.\nSpare (unconnected): IO13, IO14."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 15 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "96733aac-e717-55a4-83cd-0b0dbfb2162d")
	)
	(text "Decoupling, reset, boot, I2C pull-ups"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 137.16 0)
